Rem ==================================================================
Rem seedscribbler.shoddy — reckoner seed: scribbler.shoddy, a window
Rem held by NAME
Rem
Rem A SESSION CAN DRAW. That sentence was refused for a long time on
Rem grounds that turned out to be three different things wearing one
Rem coat, and it is worth separating them because each was answered
Rem differently.
Rem
Rem   THE HANDLE. R3.5(b): a live resource must not reach the stack,
Rem   because UNDO restores the stack and the thing naming the window
Rem   would go with it. Answered by reckoner's named-resource table —
Rem   SCRIBOPEN binds under a name the session chose, and nothing ever
Rem   pushes the window.
Rem
Rem   THE MAIN THREAD. A window has to be created and pumped on the
Rem   process's main thread, and a shell's read loop looked like it
Rem   owned that. It does not: the mill already runs the Shoddy program
Rem   on a BACKGROUND thread and keeps the main one pumping windows, so
Rem   a window opened halfway through a session is the supported path
Rem   and stays live while the prompt waits. Nothing had to change.
Rem
Rem   THE ABORTS. R3.5(a): SCRIBBLEROPEN dies when there is no window
Rem   backend, which is every way of running a program except `mill
Rem   run`. That one DID need the runtime: TRYSCRIBBLEROPEN reports it
Rem   instead, so a session in a woven binary or under the debugger is
Rem   told rather than ended.
Rem
Rem A SLOT, NOT A VALUE, and this is the one place scribbler differs
Rem from recio. A file handle is a NUMBER, so RECOPEN can put it
Rem straight in the binding. A SCRIBBLER is its own value kind and the
Rem binding has no room for one — so TRYSCRIBBLEROPEN answers a slot
Rem number, SCRIBBLEROF turns that back into the window, and
Rem SCRIBBLERSHUT lets it go. The seed holds an integer and the ordinary
Rem drawing builtins do the work, untouched.
Rem
Rem THE WORDS ARE SCRIB*, NOT SCRIBBLER*. The builtins keep their names
Rem and stay out of the dictionary — a session's SCRIBPIXEL takes a NAME
Rem where the builtin takes a window, so they are different words and a
Rem shared spelling would be a lie about which one you had.
Rem
Rem WHAT IS NOT HERE. The event words — SCRIBBLERPOLL, SCRIBBLERWAIT,
Rem SCRIBBLERSETINTERVAL — are left out on purpose and not forgotten.
Rem They exist for a frame loop, and a reckoner line is a transaction
Rem that answers and ends; a word that blocked for the next event would
Rem hold the session inside one line with no way back. Reading the mouse
Rem from a calculator prompt is a different design and not this one.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "scribbler.shoddy"
Include "cuttle.shoddy"
Include "reckoner.shoddy"
Include "seq.shoddy"

Def ScKindName() As String
    "scribbler"

Rem ---- finding the window a word was named ------------------------------

Def ScFound(word As String, st As RckState, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case RckTextArg(word, c)
        Case Ok(nm)
            ScFoundAt(word, st, nm)
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Def ScFoundAt(word As String, st As RckState, nm As String) As Result
    If Not RckBoundTo(st, nm) Then
        Err(word & ": THERE IS NOTHING OPEN CALLED " & nm, 0)
    Else
        ScFoundKind(word, First(RckResOf(st, nm)), nm)

Def ScFoundKind(word As String, r As RckRes, nm As String) As Result
    If ResKindOf(r) <> ScKindName() Then
        Err(word & ": " & nm & " IS A " & Upper(ResKindOf(r)) & ", NOT A WINDOW", 0)
    Else
        Ok(r)

Rem The slot the binding carries, turned back into the window itself.
Rem SCRIBBLEROF dies on a slot that is not open, and cannot be reached
Rem with one: the binding only exists while the window does, and CLOSE
Rem unbinds and shuts in the same breath.
Def ScWindow(r As RckRes) As Scribbler
    ScribblerOf(ResHandOf(r))

Rem ---- SCRIBOPEN --------------------------------------------------------

Def ScSeedOpen(st As RckState) As RckState
    RckReg(st, "SCRIBOPEN", 3, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => ScOpen(s, vs)), "( w h name -- )", "Open a drawing window w by h pixels and keep it open under that name. CLOSE shuts it; BOUND lists what is open. Needs a mill started with `mill run` — anything else has no window backend and is told so.")

Def ScOpen(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(RckWholeArg("SCRIBOPEN", Nth(vs, 1)), RckWholeArg("SCRIBOPEN", Nth(vs, 2)))
        Case Pair(Ok(wid), Ok(hgt))
            ScOpenNamed(st, wid, hgt, Nth(vs, 3))
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SCRIBOPEN needs a width, a height and a name")

Def ScOpenNamed(st As RckState, wid As Number, hgt As Number, nc As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("SCRIBOPEN", nc)
        Case Ok(nm)
            ScOpenFree(st, wid, hgt, nm)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SCRIBOPEN did not answer")

Def ScOpenFree(st As RckState, wid As Number, hgt As Number, nm As String) As RckWork
    If RckBoundTo(st, nm) Then
        RckWorkBad("SCRIBOPEN: THERE IS ALREADY SOMETHING OPEN CALLED " & nm)
    Else
        ScOpenSized(wid, hgt, nm)

Rem A window bigger than any screen is not refused — that is the window
Rem manager's business — but a size of nothing is, because the runtime
Rem would refuse it anyway and this way the message names the word the
Rem session typed.
Def ScOpenSized(wid As Number, hgt As Number, nm As String) As RckWork
    If wid < 1 Or hgt < 1 Then
        RckWorkBad("SCRIBOPEN: A WINDOW MUST BE AT LEAST 1 BY 1")
    Else
        ScOpenAt(wid, hgt, nm)

Def ScOpenAt(wid As Number, hgt As Number, nm As String) As RckWork
    Select Case TryScribblerOpen(wid, hgt)
        Case Ok(slot)
            RckOpened(nm, ScKindName(), slot, CutList({ CutNum(wid), CutNum(hgt) }), Fn() => ScribblerShut(slot))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad("SCRIBOPEN: " & w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SCRIBOPEN did not answer")

Rem ---- what a window can be asked ---------------------------------------

Def ScSeedAsk(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RckReg(st, "SCRIBWIDTH", 1, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => ScAsk("SCRIBWIDTH", s, vs, ScribblerWidth)), "( name -- n )", "How many pixels wide that window is.")
    Let s2 = RckReg(s1, "SCRIBHEIGHT", 1, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => ScAsk("SCRIBHEIGHT", s, vs, ScribblerHeight)), "( name -- n )", "How many pixels tall that window is.")
    RckReg(s2, "SCRIBTITLE", 2, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => ScTitle(s, vs)), "( name s -- )", "Put s in that window's title bar.")

Def ScAsk(word As String, st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell, f As [ Scribbler -- Number ]) As RckWork
    Select Case ScFound(word, st, First(vs))
        Case Ok(r)
            RckVals({ CutNum(Call(f, ScWindow(r))) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad(word & " did not answer")

Def ScTitle(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(ScFound("SCRIBTITLE", st, Nth(vs, 1)), RckTextArg("SCRIBTITLE", Nth(vs, 2)))
        Case Pair(Ok(r), Ok(s))
            ScTitled(r, s)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SCRIBTITLE needs a name and a STRING")

Rem EVERY DRAWING BUILTIN THREADS THE WINDOW BACK, so a program can
Rem chain one into the next. A registered word answers cells, not a
Rem window, so the thread has to end somewhere — it ends here. ScDrew
Rem takes the window the builtin handed back and answers nothing, which
Rem is what the session should see: the drawing happened, and there is
Rem no handle to drop.
Def ScDrew(sc As Scribbler) As RckWork
    RckVals({ })

Def ScTitled(r As RckRes, s As String) As RckWork
    ScDrew(ScribblerTitle(ScWindow(r), s))

Rem ---- drawing ----------------------------------------------------------

Rem The drawing words answer NOTHING rather than the window, which is
Rem where they part company with the builtins. A builtin threads the
Rem scribbler through so a program can chain; a session has the name and
Rem would only have to DROP what came back.

Def ScSeedDraw(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RckReg(st, "SCRIBPIXEL", 6, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => ScPixel(s, vs)), "( name x y r g b -- )", "Set one pixel. Coordinates count from 0 and are clamped to the window; colours are 0 to 255.")
    Let s2 = RckReg(s1, "SCRIBFILL", 4, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => ScFill(s, vs)), "( name r g b -- )", "Fill the whole window with one colour.")
    Let s3 = RckReg(s2, "SCRIBTEXT", 8, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => ScText(s, vs)), "( name x y scale r g b s -- )", "Draw the string s at x, y in the built-in 8x8 font, scale times its own size. A scale of 1 is eight pixels tall.")
    Let s4 = RckReg(s3, "SCRIBGETPIXEL", 3, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => ScGetPixel(s, vs)), "( name x y -- list )", "The colour at x, y as a list of red, green and blue.")
    Let s5 = RckReg(s4, "SCRIBBLIT", 1, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => ScBlit(s, vs)), "( name -- )", "Show what has been drawn. Nothing appears until this is called, which is what makes a whole picture arrive at once.")
    RckReg(s5, "SCRIBSAVE", 2, RckPureOver(Fn(s, vs) => ScSave(s, vs)), "( name path -- ok )", "Write the window to a PNG file; True on success. The one drawing word that answers something.")

Rem Every one of these reads its numbers first and touches the window
Rem only once nothing can refuse — a half-drawn shape is not an error
Rem the runtime would report, so the check has to be complete first.
Def ScPixel(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case ScFound("SCRIBPIXEL", st, Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(r)
            ScPixelAt(r, ScNums("SCRIBPIXEL", Rest(vs)))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SCRIBPIXEL did not answer")

Def ScPixelAt(r As RckRes, ns As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case ns
        Case Ok(xs)
            ScPixelDrawn(r, Nth(xs, 1), Nth(xs, 2), Nth(xs, 3), Nth(xs, 4), Nth(xs, 5))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SCRIBPIXEL did not answer")

Def ScPixelDrawn(r As RckRes, x As Number, y As Number, cr As Number, cg As Number, cb As Number) As RckWork
    ScDrew(ScribblerPixel(ScWindow(r), x, y, cr, cg, cb))

Def ScFill(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case ScFound("SCRIBFILL", st, Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(r)
            ScFillAt(r, ScNums("SCRIBFILL", Rest(vs)))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SCRIBFILL did not answer")

Def ScFillAt(r As RckRes, ns As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case ns
        Case Ok(xs)
            ScFillDrawn(r, Nth(xs, 1), Nth(xs, 2), Nth(xs, 3))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SCRIBFILL did not answer")

Def ScFillDrawn(r As RckRes, cr As Number, cg As Number, cb As Number) As RckWork
    ScDrew(ScribblerFill(ScWindow(r), cr, cg, cb))

Rem The builtin's own order is ( scribbler x y scale r g b text ), and
Rem the seed keeps it: SCALE is a real argument — the 8x8 font is tiny
Rem at 1 — and putting the STRING last is what lets a session type the
Rem numbers as a run and the words at the end.
Def ScText(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case ScFound("SCRIBTEXT", st, Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(r)
            ScTextArgs(r, ScNums("SCRIBTEXT", { Nth(vs, 2), Nth(vs, 3), Nth(vs, 4), Nth(vs, 5), Nth(vs, 6), Nth(vs, 7) }), Nth(vs, 8))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SCRIBTEXT did not answer")

Def ScTextArgs(r As RckRes, ns As Result, sc As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(ns, RckTextArg("SCRIBTEXT", sc))
        Case Pair(Ok(xs), Ok(s))
            ScTextSized(r, xs, s)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SCRIBTEXT needs a name, x, y, a scale, three colours and a STRING")

Def ScTextSized(r As RckRes, xs As List Of Number, s As String) As RckWork
    If Nth(xs, 3) < 1 Then
        RckWorkBad("SCRIBTEXT: THE SCALE MUST BE 1 OR MORE — 1 IS THE 8x8 FONT AT ITS OWN SIZE")
    Else
        ScTextDrawn(r, Nth(xs, 1), Nth(xs, 2), Nth(xs, 3), Nth(xs, 4), Nth(xs, 5), Nth(xs, 6), s)

Def ScTextDrawn(r As RckRes, x As Number, y As Number, scale As Number, cr As Number, cg As Number, cb As Number, s As String) As RckWork
    ScDrew(ScribblerText(ScWindow(r), x, y, scale, cr, cg, cb, s))

Def ScGetPixel(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case ScFound("SCRIBGETPIXEL", st, Nth(vs, 1))
        Case Ok(r)
            ScGetAt(r, ScNums("SCRIBGETPIXEL", Rest(vs)))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SCRIBGETPIXEL did not answer")

Def ScGetAt(r As RckRes, ns As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case ns
        Case Ok(xs)
            ScGotAt(r, Nth(xs, 1), Nth(xs, 2))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SCRIBGETPIXEL did not answer")

Def ScGotAt(r As RckRes, x As Number, y As Number) As RckWork
    RckVals({ CutList(Map(ToList(ScribblerGetPixel(ScWindow(r), x, y)), CutNum)) })

Def ScBlit(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case ScFound("SCRIBBLIT", st, First(vs))
        Case Ok(r)
            ScBlitted(r)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SCRIBBLIT did not answer")

Def ScBlitted(r As RckRes) As RckWork
    ScDrew(ScribblerBlit(ScWindow(r)))

Def ScSave(st As RckState, vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(ScFound("SCRIBSAVE", st, Nth(vs, 1)), RckTextArg("SCRIBSAVE", Nth(vs, 2)))
        Case Pair(Ok(r), Ok(path))
            ScSaved(r, path)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("SCRIBSAVE needs a name and a path")

Rem SCRIBBLERSAVE aborts on a path it cannot write, and there is no
Rem guarded twin — so the path is pre-flighted with TRYWRITEFILE, which
Rem both asks the question and leaves the file for the PNG to replace.
Def ScSaved(r As RckRes, path As String) As RckWork
    If Not TryWriteFile(path, "") Then
        RckVals({ CutBool(False) })
    Else
        ScSavedTo(r, path)

Def ScSavedTo(r As RckRes, path As String) As RckWork
    ScSavedOk(ScribblerSave(ScWindow(r), path))

Def ScSavedOk(sc As Scribbler) As RckWork
    RckVals({ CutBool(True) })

Rem ---- reading a list of numbers off the stack --------------------------

Rem Every drawing word takes some run of plain numbers, and each is
Rem refused whole rather than field by field, because a half-checked
Rem argument list would let the first two of five be drawn with.
Def ScNums(word As String, cs As List Of Cell) As Result
    ScNumsAt(word, cs, { })

Def ScNumsAt(word As String, cs As List Of Cell, acc As List Of Number) As Result
    If IsEmpty(cs) Then
        Ok(acc)
    Else
        ScNumsNext(word, cs, acc, First(cs))

Def ScNumsNext(word As String, cs As List Of Cell, acc As List Of Number, c As Cell) As Result
    Select Case c
        Case CutNum(x)
            ScNumsAt(word, Rest(cs), Append(acc, x))
        Case Else
            Err(RckKindWhy(word, "NUMBERs", c), 0)

Rem ---- the seed ----------------------------------------------------------

Def RckSeedScribbler(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = ScSeedOpen(RckSeeding(st, "seed-scribbler"))
    Let s2 = ScSeedAsk(s1)
    ScSeedDraw(s2)
